# tally 2.2.1 P43 S1 (L §4.4 l.669, §6.1 l.1797): the day of movements stated same, one comparison of the days each side
# can take: the booking takes the same comparison: undecided with equal amounts, the balance carries the
# window's hole and no HOLE-SAME (review g2 agent/min/b3; g2fix same/s1_dayonly pw). Before W10: a HOLE-SAME
# quoting two equal amounts beside it.
=== b3.tally
model b3
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1: money PLN
input d1: date
input d2: date
move in1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
move in2: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  d2 = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  same in1 = in2
ask s0: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask dy: m.day for m in transfers over 2026-03
ask b5: bal(konto, 2026-03-05)
ask b31: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect
b31: 600.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
b5: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a balance" (in2)
  unknown day: d2
  cut 2026-01-01
dy (m = in1): ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of in1 and in2" (in2)
  unknown day: d2
  cut 2026-01-01
s0: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
